:0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/522337797","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4810#issuecomment-522337797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4810","id":522337797,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjMzNzc5Nw==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-08-18T16:55:37Z","updated_at":"2019-08-18T16:55:37Z","body":"hi there -\r\n\r\nso the second part of your question is where I get what we are talking about most immediately.  SQlite is not storing the semantic meaning of \"REFERENCES table\", that is, it implicitly refers to the primary key , and at some point whoever wrote this code (could have been me but this code is many years old) made this odd assumption that we would link to \"lcol\" which seems wrong.\r\n\r\nso what we do is make a test.   then we have the bug, then we can fix.  Here's the test:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/test/dialect/test_sqlite.py b/test/dialect/test_sqlite.py\r\nindex 755fd6c29..fe2ecc7d3 100644\r\n--- a/test/dialect/test_sqlite.py\r\n+++ b/test/dialect/test_sqlite.py\r\n@@ -1770,10 +1770,21 @@ class ConstraintReflectionTest(fixtures.TestBase):\r\n                 \")\"\r\n             )\r\n \r\n+            conn.execute(\r\n+                \"CREATE TABLE implicit_referred (pk integer primary key)\"\r\n+            )\r\n+            # no column given\r\n+            conn.execute(\r\n+                \"CREATE TABLE implicit_referrer \"\r\n+                \"(id integer REFERENCES implicit_referred)\"\r\n+            )\r\n+\r\n     @classmethod\r\n     def teardown_class(cls):\r\n         with testing.db.begin() as conn:\r\n             for name in [\r\n+                \"implicit_referrer\",\r\n+                \"implicit_referred\",\r\n                 \"m\",\r\n                 \"main.l\",\r\n                 \"k\",\r\n@@ -1892,6 +1903,23 @@ class ConstraintReflectionTest(fixtures.TestBase):\r\n             ],\r\n         )\r\n \r\n+    def test_foreign_key_implicit_parent(self):\r\n+        inspector = Inspector(testing.db)\r\n+        fks = inspector.get_foreign_keys(\"implicit_referrer\")\r\n+        eq_(\r\n+            fks,\r\n+            [\r\n+                {\r\n+                    \"name\": None,\r\n+                    \"constrained_columns\": [\"id\"],\r\n+                    \"referred_schema\": None,\r\n+                    \"referred_table\": \"implicit_referred\",\r\n+                    \"referred_columns\": [\"pk\"],\r\n+                    \"options\": {},\r\n+                }\r\n+            ],\r\n+        )\r\n+\r\n     def test_unnamed_inline_foreign_key(self):\r\n         inspector = Inspector(testing.db)\r\n         fks = inspector.get_foreign_keys(\"e\")\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nhow did I make that test?   I first created the table with REFERENCES\r\nimplicit_referred(pk),  then got the assertion to pass, then I took out the\r\n(pk) part and confirmed the assertion failed.  so now we have a failing test\r\nand we have to figure out how to get that \"pk\" back. unfortunately it looks\r\nlike we have to go out and reflect the other table's PKs, which is silly that\r\nSQLite would make us do this, but at least SQLite is extremely fast so\r\nshouldn't be an issue:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/sqlite/base.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/sqlite/base.py\r\nindex 9a0455a9d..cfe3197ed 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/sqlite/base.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/sqlite/base.py\r\n@@ -1755,7 +1755,8 @@ class SQLiteDialect(default.DefaultDialect):\r\n             (numerical_id, rtbl, lcol, rcol) = (row[0], row[2], row[3], row[4])\r\n \r\n             if rcol is None:\r\n-                rcol = lcol\r\n+                referred_pk = self.get_pk_constraint(connection, rtbl, schema=schema)\r\n+                rcol = referred_pk['constrained_columns'][0]\r\n \r\n             if self._broken_fk_pragma_quotes:\r\n                 rtbl = re.sub(r\"^[\\\"\\[`\\']|[\\\"\\]`\\']$\", \"\", rtbl)\r\n```\r\n\r\nthat will fix this case but doesn't cover the case for a composite primary key.\r\n  The patch  I will push up will accommodate for that case also as it has to\r\nnot hardcode that zero in  there.  thanks for the bug report.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/522337797/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2564564069,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI1NjQ1NjQwNjk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/2564564069","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/u